    "created_at": "2026-01-22T15:34:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-22T15:34:22Z",
    "body": "Making `data:` URLs not be secure contexts seems weird and wrong. After all, what a secure context is about is whether the document found at the URL in question could have been tampered with or read in transit.\nThis is not the case for `data:` URLs because no data is being transmitted anywhere so the document that opens is the document available at that URL, always and there is no transit for it to be intercepted in.\n\nI also like using `data:` URLs for simple reproductions when reporting bugs in Ladybird and I'd hate for that to be impossible with APIs that require a secure context.",
