    "updated_at": "2026-01-22T17:01:02Z",
    "body": "I don't really have an opinion either way here. Data URLs are a bit weird, and it does not seem particularly strange to me for them to not be secure context considering they have an opaque origin. Then again, file:// URLs in most contexts have an opaque origin, yet they are allowed in secureContext.\n\n> I also like using data: URLs for simple reproductions when reporting bugs in Ladybird and I'd hate for that to be impossible with APIs that require a secure context.\n\nSince other browsers already behave in this way for one reason or another, I think this is already effectively the case since reductions are most useful when the behavior is compared against other browsers.\n\nhttps://github.com/w3c/webappsec-secure-contexts/issues/69 seems to be the most related previous issue surrounding this, but I haven't quite been able to follow all of the issue links about the conclusions.",
